{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwaDooM6QyknRxvcawJy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a `contract` project to `vitest.config.ts`. It runs `test/contract/**/*.test.{js,ts}` with `extends: false`. I haven't run anything yet: the command to list each project's tests needed your approval, so I skipped it.\n\n**Why `extends: false` matters:** the stub is loaded by the root-level `setupFiles: [\"./test/stub-fetch.ts\"]`. In Vitest 5 (you have 5.0.3), inline projects inherit the root config by default. If I'd left out `extends`, the contract project would quietly load the stub too. Its tests would then check the fixture file instead of the real API and still pass. Setting `extends: false` stops it inheriting, so it uses the real `fetch`. I left a comment in the config explaining this so nobody removes it later.\n\n**Unit project:** unchanged. It still has `extends: true` and the same `include` pattern, so it keeps the stub.\n\nTo confirm it works:\n- `npx vitest run --project contract` should make real network calls.\n- `npx vitest run --project unit` should behave exactly as before.\n\nPlain `npm test` now runs both projects, so it will hit the live API. If you want CI to stay offline, have it run `vitest run --project unit` instead."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_read_input_tokens":25168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":322},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a99d570-3f1c-4009-b2b2-32f72152304b","uuid":"0caf4cdc-9733-4cdb-9a95-5a142a426ec0","timestamp":"2026-10-12T02:43:15.476Z","request_id":"req_011CfwaDoXiamR1PvAJ1ieAD"}
